  "method": "Plan-view SHAPE computed from the Main Injector TDR (src:fermilab-geo-mi-tdr-1994), then PLACED on the ground by fitting it to an OpenStreetMap service road; neither the tunnel nor the ring is traced in OSM. (1) Lattice from the TDR: eight straight sections in the order MI-60, -62, -10, -22, -30, -32, -40, -52 with lengths 138, 52, 69, 52, 138, 52, 69, 52 m (ch. 2 s2.1: 'Straight sections MI-10 and MI-40 are 69 m long (two cells), straight sections MI-22, -32, -52, and -62 are 52 m long (one and one half cells), and straight sections MI-30 and MI-60 are 138 m long (four cells)'), each flanked on both sides by 4 dispersion-suppressor half-cells of 12.9665 m (two 4.1 m dipoles each); the arcs are made of normal half-cells of 17.2886 m (two 6.1 m dipoles each). The number of normal half-cells between successive straights is 2, 12, 38, 2 for each half ring (counted from the dipole positions in the MAD lattice listing in the TDR's appendix; the second half repeats it by the TDR's 'twofold rotational symmetry'). Summed length 3319.414 m against the TDR's 'Circumference 3319.419 m' (Table 1-1). (2) Bending: the dipoles (216 x 6.1 m + 128 x 4.1 m, one 'Dipole Field 17.2 kG') are treated as one field, so each bends by its length / rho with rho = 1842.4 m / 2 pi = 293.2 m; heading was integrated along the sequence (bend spread evenly over each half-cell). The path closes on itself. (3) Self-check against a TDR statement that was NOT used to build the shape: 'The line from MI-52 to MI-62 is offset 28.789277 m from the MI-60 straight section and parallel to it'; the reconstruction gives offsets of 28.74 m and 28.89 m (mean 28.82 m, 0.1% from the TDR) and a direction within 0.02 degrees of MI-60. (4) Placement: one rigid rotation and translation (no scaling), chosen so that OSM way 21813770 'Indian Creek Road' (a private service road that encircles the ring) stays at a constant distance outside it: trimmed least squares (70% of the 2.9 km road; the two tails that leave the ring are trimmed) gives a standard deviation of 3.7 m about a mean offset of 40 m, and a 10 m shift raises it to 5-8 m; the mirror-image shape fits worse (7.0 m). Checks not used in the fit: the OSM building 'MI-62' (way 272687522) has its centroid 9 m from the derived centre of the MI-62 straight section; the TDR puts the MI-60 straight 11.823 m from the Tevatron F0 straight, and the fitted MI-60 line lies 1025.9 m from the centre of the Tevatron circle drawn on this map (R + 11.823 = 1014.5 m; that circle is itself accurate to about 60 m). A ring road is a proxy for the tunnel, so accuracy_m is 30 (the ring-road tier). Sampled every 12 m (278 vertices, chord error 0.06 m); haversine on R = 6371008.8 m measures 3319.37 m.",
